        },
        "parms": "# midiout, midiformat and sxformat — raw MIDI out\nmidiout sends MIDI messages to an output port. Each list it receives is one message, written as byte values: 144 60 100 is a note-on for middle C. It also takes the messages noteon and the other builders make. Its argument is the port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them.\nmidiformat builds messages as lists of numbers, so you can read them: the opposite of midiparse. sxformat builds a system-exclusive (SysEx) message, a device's own data, from a template.\nMax's midiout sends each number it receives as one byte. Here midiout sends whole messages: a list is one message, and a single number is not sent.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
