      "object 23": {
        "ID": 23,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "220.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "1. A list made in the patch goes straight to midiout. Click 144: append puts 60 100 after it, and midiout sends 144 60 100 as one note-on. 128 makes its note-off. One list is one message, so give each message a list of its own.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 24": {
        "ID": 24,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "360.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. midiformat's inlets, left to right: note, key pressure, controller, program, channel pressure, pitch bend and channel. Click 60: append makes 60 100, and the list box shows 144 60 100. A bare number is sent with 0: 62 is a release, sent as a note-on with velocity 0, and 64 is controller 64, the sustain pedal, at 0. 6 is program 6, sent as 5: midiformat counts programs from 1. Click 2, and the messages after it go to channel 2.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 25": {
        "ID": 25,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "560.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. sxformat 240 125 $i1 $i2 247 fills its placeholders from its inlets, and the left one sends. Click 64, then 1: 240 125 1 64 247. A list on the left inlet fills $i1, $i2 and so on, then sends. Start a SysEx message with 240 and end it with 247; sxformat does not add them. 125 is the ID kept for non-commercial use, so no maker's device should act on these.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 26": {
        "ID": 26,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "760.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. A negative value leaves its byte out: click -1, then 7, for 240 125 7 247. sum is a checksum, as Roland devices want: the byte that makes everything after sumstart add up to a multiple of 128. Click 32, then 16: 16 + 32 + 80 = 128, so 240 125 16 32 80 247.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
