        "parms": "6. xmidiin 0 shows each message that arrives on input port 0 as numbers, one list per message, and print writes every one to the log (Ctrl+J). 144 60 100 comes back as it was sent. On Linux, output 0 and input 0 are usually Midi Through, which sends back whatever it receives, so you see what you send. Elsewhere, set both arguments to a loopback port.",
